Article 2 Where the following circumstances exist concurrently, the People's Court shall determine that the debtor is unable to discharge due debts:
(1) the creditor-debtor relationship is established according to law;
(2) the time limit for performance of the debt has expired;
(3) the debtor has not fully discharged the debt.

Article 4 Where the debtor's book assets are greater than its liabilities, but any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Court shall determine that it is obviously lacking in ability to discharge debts:
(1) it is unable to discharge debts due to serious shortage of funds or inability to realize property;
(2) the legal representative's whereabouts are unknown and no other person is responsible for managing the property, so the debts cannot be discharged;
(3) after compulsory execution by the People's Court, the debts cannot be discharged;
(4) long-term losses and difficulty in turning around operations make it impossible to discharge debts;
(5) other circumstances causing the debtor to lose its ability to discharge debts.
